  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Authorization applies everywhere",
      "items": [
        "A route practiceId, stale client role or hidden button grants nothing. Every read/write/job/source/file/export resolves current capability and ownership.",
        "Administrator has no implicit clinical access. Scheduler sees minimum identity/contact; registration needs both SCHEDULE_MANAGE and PATIENT_REGISTER. Patient gets only their record link and curated publications. An adversarial isolation matrix measures the cross-practice, capability and patient cases in API verify (story 1.4)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Session and device decisions — ADR-008 and ADR-010 accepted",
      "items": [
        "Web/PWA: secure host-only opaque cookie and CSRF, no bearer in browser storage. Native: same opaque server session over the Authorization header after credential verification to a registered device; platform secure storage only.",
        "No mixed transports; a bearer request carrying a cookie or browser origin headers is refused. Revoke on logout, reset and suspension; device registration can be revoked. Native duration and the exact header rule remain story 10.5 checks. Built: the web cookie session with CSRF, revocation on recovery and the refusal of any Bearer header; the native transport and devices are planned."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Contract and client compatibility — ADR-009 accepted",
      "items": [
        "One OpenAPI source and generated TypeScript client; additive /api/v1 evolution, X-Client-Version and minimum-version policy; outdated clients show an update screen.",
        "The contract (0.5.0-planning) declares 100 operations and 23 are served. getApiMeta, getHistorySummary, listDemoScenarios and resetSyntheticDemo were added since the first snapshot. The four native/device operations and CLIENT_TOO_OLD / 426 (story 10.4) are not yet declared. Compatibility window numbers remain an assumption."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Device and database limits",
      "items": [
        "The service worker caches the application shell only; no clinical cache at rest. Push is content-free, reauthorized at delivery and revoked with device access. Offline clinical mode, native practitioner UI and biometric controls are deferred.",
        "Identity/bootstrap lookup and job discovery use narrow metadata access, then establish context. Domain queries use the same physical connection and transaction-local RLS; migration credentials never reach HTTP runtime. RLS alone is not clinical authorization."
      ]
    }
  ]
